---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

// The five steps of the mechanic, in the order an incident actually runs
// through them. The order is the argument: you cannot detect what you never
// observed, and you cannot quarantine on a signal nobody can investigate
// afterwards. Each one names the concrete thing underneath it.
const flow = [
  {
    n: '01', name: 'Observe',
    line: 'Every action an agent takes crosses Kyde.',
    body: 'One line of configuration in front of the model, no code changes in the agent. It records everything and blocks nothing until you decide otherwise.',
  },
  {
    n: '02', name: 'Detect',
    line: "Behavior is measured against the agent's own baseline.",
    body: 'Not a content filter. What the agent does: which tools it reaches for, which systems it touches, how often, how long it runs, and how far that has moved from the way it worked before.',
  },
  {
    n: '03', name: 'Quarantine',
    line: 'A deviating agent loses reach before it does damage.',
    body: 'Autonomy is cut back for a high-risk agent at the boundary, rather than after somebody notices it in a support ticket three weeks later.',
  },
  {
    n: '04', name: 'Investigate',
    line: 'Reconstruct what actually happened.',
    body: "The record is written at the boundary, outside the agent's control, so a deviation can be traced through the actions that produced it instead of guessed at.",
  },
  {
    n: '05', name: 'Prove',
    line: 'Show a third party, without us in the room.',
    body: 'Hash-chained and signed as it is written, exported as a dated document your auditor recomputes on their own machine.',
  },
];

// Organization and WebSite schema live on the home page, which is now the
// platform page. The description leads with the layer and names the build
// service second, in the order the site itself now argues them.
const orgSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Organization",
  name: "Kyde",
  url: "https://kyde.com",
  logo: "https://kyde.com/kyde-logo.svg",
  description: "Kyde detects behavioral drift in AI agents. Every action crosses Kyde, is measured against the agent's own baseline, and a deviating agent can be quarantined before the deviation becomes an incident, on a zero trust enforcement layer in the customer's own environment.",
};

const websiteSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebSite",
  name: "Kyde",
  url: "https://kyde.com",
};
---

<Base
  title="KYDE, Behavioral Drift Detection for AI Agents"
  description="AI agents drift. Kyde watches what your agents actually do, detects the deviation, and can quarantine them before it becomes an incident, whether they go off on their own, are pushed off course by prompt injection, or get stuck in a loop burning money. On a zero trust enforcement layer in your own infrastructure."
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(orgSchema)} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(websiteSchema)} />
  </Fragment>
  <Navbar />

  <main>
    <!-- ══════════ HERO STAGE ══════════ -->
    <!-- The stage came over from the workers page when the two swapped places.
         It was always a picture of this argument rather than of the build
         service: unordered agents drift, cross a gate, and come out in a
         lattice. It belongs to the page that sells the gate. -->
    <section class="relative overflow-hidden min-h-screen flex flex-col justify-center pt-28 pb-16 bg-bg-0">
      <canvas id="hero-datastream" class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
      <div class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none hero-noise"></div>
      <div class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none bg-gradient-to-r from-bg-0 via-bg-0/45 to-transparent"></div>
      <div class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none bg-gradient-to-b from-transparent via-transparent to-bg-0"></div>

      <div class="relative max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 w-full">
        <!-- Category register. The regulation line moved down to the terminal:
             it is why a buyer signs, but it is not why they read on, and the
             page now opens on the problem rather than on the compliance frame. -->
        <p id="hero-eyebrow" class="mb-4 md:mb-5 font-mono text-[10px] md:text-[11px] text-white/55 uppercase tracking-[0.16em] md:tracking-[0.2em]" style="opacity:0;transition:opacity 0.9s ease;">
          Behavioral drift detection for AI agents
        </p>
        <!-- The problem, then us. Own Your Intelligence was well branded and
             said nothing a reader could act on; it survives as the closing
             argument at the bottom of the page. Two lines of equal length,
             which is what makes the scramble land. -->
        <h1 class="hero-h1 text-[2rem] text-white uppercase tracking-tight leading-none sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl lg:text-7xl" style="opacity:0;">
          <span id="hero-l1" style="display:block">AI Agents Drift.</span>
          <span id="hero-l2" style="display:block">Kyde Detects It.</span>
        </h1>
        <p id="hero-sub" class="mt-5 md:mt-6 text-sm md:text-base lg:text-lg text-white uppercase tracking-[0.12em] leading-snug max-w-xs md:max-w-md lg:max-w-xl" style="opacity:0;transition:opacity 0.9s ease;">
          How do you know an agent is still behaving the way it was supposed to?
        </p>
        <p id="hero-explainer" class="mt-3 text-sm md:text-base text-white/70 leading-snug max-w-xs md:max-w-md lg:max-w-xl" style="opacity:0;transition:opacity 0.9s ease 0.15s;">
          Kyde watches what your agents actually do. When they drift, we detect it and can quarantine them, whether they go off on their own, get pushed off course by prompt injection, or get stuck in a loop burning money.
        </p>
        <div id="hero-ctas" class="mt-7 flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4" style="opacity:0;transition:opacity 0.9s ease 0.5s;">
          <button
            onclick="openModal()"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-white text-cta-ink px-6 py-3.5 text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-[0.1em] hover:bg-cta-hover transition-all"
          >
            Become a design partner →
          </button>
          <a
            href="/behavioral-drift"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border border-white/40 text-white px-6 py-3.5 text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-[0.1em] hover:border-white hover:bg-white/10 transition-all"
          >
            Read the research →
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-7 space-y-1.5" style="opacity:0;transition:opacity 0.9s ease 0.7s;" id="hero-terminal">
          <p class="font-mono text-[10px] md:text-[11px] text-white/45 uppercase tracking-[0.18em]">On-premise <span class="text-white/20">·</span> Private cloud <span class="text-white/20">·</span> EU-hosted</p>
          <p class="font-mono text-[10px] md:text-[11px] text-white/45 uppercase tracking-[0.18em]">Built for GDPR <span class="text-white/20">·</span> EU AI Act <span class="text-white/20">·</span> NIS-2 <span class="text-white/20">·</span> DORA</p>
          <!-- two registers only: where it runs, what it is built against. The
               five steps were here too and repeated the section directly below. -->
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

<script>
  const CHARS = "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789";
  const SPEED = 0.22;

  function scrambleLine(el: HTMLElement, target: string, delay: number, onDone?: () => void) {
    let frame = 0;
    setTimeout(() => {
      el.innerText = target;
      const finalH = el.offsetHeight;
      el.style.height = finalH + "px";
      el.style.overflow = "hidden";

      function tick() {
        let out = "";
        for (let i = 0; i < target.length; i++) {
          if (i < frame) {
            out += target[i];
          } else if (target[i] === " " || target[i] === ".") {
            out += target[i];
          } else {
            out += CHARS[Math.floor(Math.random() * CHARS.length)];
          }
        }
        el.innerText = out;
        frame += SPEED;
        if (frame < target.length) {
          requestAnimationFrame(tick);
        } else {
          el.innerText = target;
          el.style.height = "";
          el.style.overflow = "";
          if (onDone) onDone();
        }
      }
      tick();
    }, delay);
  }

  const l1 = document.getElementById("hero-l1") as HTMLElement;
  const l2 = document.getElementById("hero-l2") as HTMLElement;
  const sub = document.getElementById("hero-sub") as HTMLElement;
  const eyebrow = document.getElementById("hero-eyebrow") as HTMLElement;
  const h1 = l1?.closest("h1") as HTMLElement;
  if (h1) { h1.style.animation = "none"; h1.style.opacity = "0"; }
  const explainer = document.getElementById("hero-explainer") as HTMLElement;
  const ctas = document.getElementById("hero-ctas") as HTMLElement;
  if (l1) scrambleLine(l1, "AI AGENTS DRIFT.", 200);
  if (l2) scrambleLine(l2, "KYDE DETECTS IT.", 200, () => {
    if (eyebrow) eyebrow.style.opacity = "1";
    if (sub) sub.style.opacity = "1";
    if (explainer) explainer.style.opacity = "1";
    if (ctas) ctas.style.opacity = "1";
    const term = document.getElementById("hero-terminal");
    if (term) term.style.opacity = "1";
  });
  setTimeout(() => { if (h1) h1.style.opacity = "1"; }, 200);

  // ── Boundary-gate figure ────────────────────────────────────────
  // Geometric, not "rain": unordered agents drift on the left,
  // cross the vertical gate line, and snap into a strict lattice , 
  // ungoverned chaos becomes governed order. Rare green pulse at
  // crossing (recorded), rare red flash bouncing off (blocked).
  const canvas = document.getElementById("hero-datastream") as HTMLCanvasElement | null;
  const reduced = window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches;

  if (canvas) {
    const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d")!;
    let W = 0, H = 0, GATE = 0, ROW = 26;

    // Theme-aware palette: the figure is drawn from CSS tokens, not literal
    // rgb triples, so it inverts cleanly (light ink on dark, dark ink on
    // light) instead of staying a fixed dark box when the theme toggles.
    const C = { ink: "242,242,242", live: "61,220,132", alert: "255,92,92", light: false };
    function hexToRgb(hex: string): string {
      const m = hex.trim().replace("#", "");
      const n = parseInt(m.length === 3 ? m.split("").map((c) => c + c).join("") : m, 16);
      return `${(n >> 16) & 255},${(n >> 8) & 255},${n & 255}`;
    }
    function readColors() {
      const cs = getComputedStyle(document.documentElement);
      C.ink = hexToRgb(cs.getPropertyValue("--color-ink-0") || "#F2F2F2");
      C.live = hexToRgb(cs.getPropertyValue("--color-live") || "#3DDC84");
      C.alert = hexToRgb(cs.getPropertyValue("--color-alert") || "#FF5C5C");
      // A bloom is emitted light. On a dark ground it brightens toward ink; on
      // paper the same stops paint a grey smudge, so it has to tint toward the
      // accent instead. Everything downstream branches on this one flag.
      const bg = hexToRgb(cs.getPropertyValue("--color-bg-0") || "#050505").split(",").map(Number);
      C.light = (bg[0] * 0.299 + bg[1] * 0.587 + bg[2] * 0.114) > 128;
    }
    readColors();

    function hash(n: number): number {
      let t = (n + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0;
      t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);
      t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);
      return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;
    }

    type P = {
      x: number; y: number; vx: number; seed: number;
      state: "wild" | "signed" | "blocked";
      rowY: number; pulse: number;
    };
    let parts: P[] = [];

    // occasional bloom when a particle crosses the gate
    type Flare = { x: number; y: number; t0: number };
    let flares: Flare[] = [];
    let lastFlare = 0;

    function spawn(p: P, i: number, initial = false) {
      p.x = initial ? hash(i * 7 + 1) * GATE : -10 - hash(i * 13) * 60;
      p.y = 40 + hash(i * 31 + performance.now() % 9973) * (H - 80);
      p.vx = 12 + hash(i * 17) * 22;
      p.seed = i * 7919 + Math.floor(performance.now());
      p.state = "wild";
      p.pulse = 0;
    }

    // Measuring once at script time is not enough: on a reload the module can run
    // before layout has settled, and a canvas that is measured at zero keeps its
    // default 300x150 buffer while CSS stretches it to full width. Everything then
    // looks scaled up and, because the particles cross a much smaller space, far
    // too fast. Only a real window resize used to fix it.
    function resize() {
      const w = canvas.clientWidth;
      const h = canvas.clientHeight;
      if (!w || !h) return;                       // not laid out yet, try again later
      const dpr = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);
      if (w === W && h === H && canvas.width === Math.round(w * dpr)) return;
      W = w;
      H = h;
      canvas.width = Math.round(W * dpr);
      canvas.height = Math.round(H * dpr);
      ctx.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);
      GATE = W * 0.68;
      parts = [];
      const n = Math.max(40, Math.floor(W / 16));
      for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        const p = {} as P;
        spawn(p, i, true);
        parts.push(p);
      }
    }

    let last = 0;
    function draw(t: number) {
      const dt = Math.min((t - last) / 1000, 0.05) || 0.016;
      last = t;
      ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);

      // lattice on the governed side, faint, strict
      ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(${C.ink},${C.light ? 0.16 : 0.08})`;
      for (let x = GATE + ROW; x < W; x += ROW)
        for (let y = ROW; y < H; y += ROW)
          ctx.fillRect(x - 0.75, y - 0.75, 1.5, 1.5);

      // gate line, nearly invisible at the ends, a faint shimmer mid-height;
      // it reveals itself through interaction (blooms, blocks), not presence
      const gateGrad = ctx.createLinearGradient(0, 0, 0, H);
      gateGrad.addColorStop(0, `rgba(${C.ink},0)`);
      gateGrad.addColorStop(0.5, `rgba(${C.ink},${C.light ? 0.22 : 0.13})`);
      gateGrad.addColorStop(1, `rgba(${C.ink},0)`);
      ctx.fillStyle = gateGrad;
      ctx.fillRect(GATE, 0, 1, H);
      for (let y = 0; y < H; y += ROW * 2) {
        const env = Math.sin((Math.PI * y) / H);
        ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(${C.ink},${(C.light ? 0.26 : 0.16) * env * env})`;
        ctx.fillRect(GATE - 3, y, 7, 1);
      }

      for (const p of parts) {
        const jitterSeed = p.seed + Math.floor(t / 300);

        if (p.state === "wild") {
          // brownian drift with slow right bias
          p.x += p.vx * dt;
          p.y += (hash(jitterSeed) - 0.5) * 34 * dt * 2.2;

          if (p.x >= GATE) {
            if (hash(p.seed + 5) > 0.93) {
              p.state = "blocked";
              p.pulse = 1;
              p.vx = -18;
            } else {
              p.state = "signed";
              p.pulse = hash(p.seed + 9) > 0.7 ? 1 : 0;
              p.rowY = Math.round(p.y / ROW) * ROW;
              p.vx = 26 + hash(p.seed + 3) * 18;
              // every few seconds, one crossing blooms
              if (t - lastFlare > 2100 && hash(p.seed + 11) > 0.4) {
                flares.push({ x: GATE, y: p.rowY, t0: t });
                lastFlare = t;
              }
            }
          }
          ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(${C.ink},${C.light ? 0.42 : 0.32})`;
          ctx.fillRect(p.x - 1, p.y - 1, 2, 2);
        } else if (p.state === "signed") {
          p.x += p.vx * dt;
          p.y += (p.rowY - p.y) * Math.min(dt * 6, 1); // snap to lattice row

          if (p.pulse > 0) {
            ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(${C.live},${p.pulse * 0.7})`;
            ctx.lineWidth = 1;
            ctx.strokeRect(p.x - 4, p.y - 4, 8, 8);
            p.pulse -= dt * 1.4;
          }
          ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(${C.ink},${C.light ? 0.82 : 0.68})`;
          ctx.fillRect(p.x - 1, p.y - 1, 2, 2);

          if (p.x > W + 10) spawn(p, Math.floor(p.seed / 7919));
        } else {
          // blocked: red flash at the gate, drift back, fade
          p.x += p.vx * dt;
          if (p.pulse > 0) {
            ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(${C.alert},${p.pulse * 0.8})`;
            ctx.lineWidth = 1;
            ctx.beginPath();
            ctx.moveTo(p.x + 4, p.y - 4); ctx.lineTo(p.x - 4, p.y + 4);
            ctx.moveTo(p.x - 4, p.y - 4); ctx.lineTo(p.x + 4, p.y + 4);
            ctx.stroke();
            p.pulse -= dt * 0.9;
          } else {
            spawn(p, Math.floor(p.seed / 7919));
          }
        }
      }

      // flares, soft light bloom at the gate, expanding and fading
      flares = flares.filter((f) => t - f.t0 < 1600);
      for (const f of flares) {
        const age = (t - f.t0) / 1600; // 0 → 1
        const ease = 1 - Math.pow(1 - age, 2);
        const r = 16 + ease * 130;
        const a = (1 - age) * 0.85;

        const g = ctx.createRadialGradient(f.x, f.y, 0, f.x, f.y, r);
        if (C.light) {
          g.addColorStop(0, `rgba(${C.live},${a * 0.55})`);
          g.addColorStop(0.25, `rgba(${C.live},${a * 0.22})`);
          g.addColorStop(0.6, `rgba(${C.live},${a * 0.08})`);
          g.addColorStop(1, `rgba(${C.live},0)`);
        } else {
          g.addColorStop(0, `rgba(${C.ink},${a})`);
          g.addColorStop(0.25, `rgba(${C.ink},${a * 0.35})`);
          g.addColorStop(0.6, `rgba(${C.live},${a * 0.22})`);
          g.addColorStop(1, `rgba(${C.live},0)`);
        }
        ctx.fillStyle = g;
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(f.x, f.y, r, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.fill();

        // bright core that snuffs out quickly
        if (age < 0.35) {
          ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(${C.ink},${(1 - age / 0.35) * 0.9})`;
          ctx.fillRect(f.x - 2, f.y - 2, 4, 4);
        }

        // brief brightening of the gate line around the bloom
        const gl = ctx.createLinearGradient(f.x, f.y - r, f.x, f.y + r);
        gl.addColorStop(0, `rgba(${C.ink},0)`);
        gl.addColorStop(0.5, `rgba(${C.ink},${a * 0.8})`);
        gl.addColorStop(1, `rgba(${C.ink},0)`);
        ctx.fillStyle = gl;
        ctx.fillRect(GATE, f.y - r, 1, r * 2);
      }
    }

    resize();
    window.addEventListener("resize", resize);

    // Held in a variable on purpose: an observer with no reference of its own can
    // be collected, and then it silently stops firing. Measured that happening.
    const canvasObserver = "ResizeObserver" in window ? new ResizeObserver(() => resize()) : null;
    if (canvasObserver) canvasObserver.observe(canvas);

    // Belt and braces for the first paint. The observer covers later changes, but
    // the very first measurement can land before layout is final, and the guard
    // above makes each of these free once the size is already right.
    requestAnimationFrame(() => resize());
    window.addEventListener("load", () => resize());
    if (document.fonts && document.fonts.ready) document.fonts.ready.then(() => resize());

    // Re-read the palette on theme toggle. The running rAF loop repaints
    // every frame anyway and will pick the new colors up on its own; the
    // reduced-motion path only ever draws once, so it needs an explicit nudge.
    window.addEventListener("kyde:theme", () => {
      readColors();
      if (reduced) draw(performance.now());
    });

    if (reduced) {
      draw(1);
    } else {
      let heroVisible = true;
      new IntersectionObserver((es) => { heroVisible = es[0].isIntersecting; }).observe(canvas);
      const loop = (t: number) => { if (heroVisible) draw(t); requestAnimationFrame(loop); };
      requestAnimationFrame(loop);
    }
  }
</script>


    <!-- ══════════ 01 · THE MECHANIC ══════════ -->
    <!-- Directly under the hero, because the hero makes a claim and a reader who
         came from a message that made the same claim wants the shape of it
         before anything else. Laid out left to right: this is a path an incident
         travels, not a list of modules, and the order carries the argument. -->
    <section class="bg-bg-0">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 md:py-20 md:border-x md:border-line-0">
        <div class="flex items-end justify-between border-b border-line-0 pb-3 mb-10">
          <span class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink-1">01 · The mechanic</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight leading-[1.03] text-ink-0 mb-8 max-w-3xl">
          Know what your agents are actually doing.
        </h2>
        <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4 mb-12">
          <p class="text-lg text-ink-1 leading-relaxed">
            Every action crosses Kyde. We build a behavioral baseline for each agent and continuously test what actually happens against it.
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-ink-1 leading-relaxed">
            When behavior changes, Kyde detects the deviation. A high-risk agent can be quarantined before that deviation becomes an incident. The record underneath stays available for investigation and for independent verification.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mb-px hidden lg:flex items-center gap-3 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-ink-2 pb-4">
          <span class="text-ink-0">Agent action</span>
          <span class="flex-1 h-px bg-line-0"></span>
          <span>Observe</span><span class="text-ink-2/50">→</span>
          <span>Detect</span><span class="text-ink-2/50">→</span>
          <span class="text-ember">Quarantine</span><span class="text-ink-2/50">→</span>
          <span>Investigate</span>
          <span class="flex-1 h-px bg-line-0"></span>
          <span class="text-live">Prove</span>
        </div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5 border-t border-l border-line-0">
          {flow.map(({ n, name, line, body }) => (
            <div class="border-r border-b border-line-0 px-5 py-6 md:px-6 md:py-7">
              <div class="flex items-baseline gap-2 mb-4">
                <span class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-2">{n}</span>
                <span class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-gold">{name}</span>
              </div>
              <p class="text-base md:text-lg text-ink-0 leading-snug mb-3">{line}</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-1 leading-relaxed">{body}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="mt-8 text-base text-ink-1 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
          You do not have to start at step three. Observe first: point one agent at the gateway, block nothing, and in week one you already know what your agents do, what leaves your house, and what it costs. Enforcement is a switch you flip when you are ready.
        </p>

        <!-- The picture of the whole claim, and the only one on the page that
             shows time passing. Every other figure is a topology: what sits
             where. Drift is not a topology, it is a line leaving a band, so it
             gets a plot. The ghost continuation is the point of the figure, not
             decoration: it is the incident that did not happen. -->
        <div class="mt-14 border border-line-0 bg-bg-1 px-5 py-5 md:px-8 md:py-7">
          <div class="flex items-end justify-between border-b border-line-0 pb-3 mb-6">
            <span class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink-2">One agent, watched across its runs</span>
            <span class="fig-label">FIG.1</span>
          </div>
          <svg id="drift-fig" viewBox="0 0 1000 330" class="w-full h-auto" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M6 21 L6 6 L21 6"       fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink-0)" stroke-opacity="0.45" stroke-width="1" />
            <path d="M979 6 L994 6 L994 21"  fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink-0)" stroke-opacity="0.45" stroke-width="1" />
